│ musculoskeletal disorders and for nonspecific pain in the upper limbs. The overlap and impact on daily activities    │
│ and healthcare utilization were explored.   Results Among 6,038 first‐stage responders, 3,152 reported upper limb    │
│ symptoms and 1,960 were subsequently examined. Of subjects with pain, 44.8% had 1 or more specific soft‐tissue       │
│ disorders. Site‐specific prevalence rates were as follows: shoulder tendinitis 4.5% among men and 6.1% among women;  │
│ adhesive capsulitis 8.2% among men and 10.1% among women; lateral epicondylitis 1.3% among men and 1.1% among women; │
│ de Quervain\'s disease 0.5% among men and 1.3% among women; other tenosynovitis of the hand or wrist, 1.1% among men │
